1
00:01:00,945 --> 00:01:02,225
<i>Runch, if your happiness</i>

2
00:01:02,305 --> 00:01:04,305
<i>comes at the cost of treating me horribly,</i>

3
00:01:04,385 --> 00:01:08,305
I won't back down. There's no way
I'm losing you to that girl.

4
00:01:08,385 --> 00:01:12,745
<i>Today's event feels so sweet and warm,</i>
<i>as if it was a family party.</i>

5
00:01:12,825 --> 00:01:14,505
They humiliated you,

6
00:01:14,585 --> 00:01:16,665
<i>so you've got to do the same.</i>

7
00:01:19,265 --> 00:01:20,305
Stop it, Mom!

8
00:01:20,385 --> 00:01:21,585
What the hell are you doing?!

9
00:01:22,985 --> 00:01:26,185
That old hag needs to learn
that she can't just slap anyone.

10
00:01:26,265 --> 00:01:27,745
Come on, then, you little brat!

11
00:01:27,825 --> 00:01:29,145
-That's enough, Mom!
-Come on.

12
00:01:35,025 --> 00:01:37,585
I never imagined
you'd go this far to hurt me.

13
00:01:38,105 --> 00:01:39,785
I never imagined

14
00:01:39,865 --> 00:01:42,385
you'd go this far to hurt my wife either.

15
00:01:43,105 --> 00:01:44,905
I'm just standing up for myself.

16
00:01:44,985 --> 00:01:46,145
If I don't fight,

17
00:01:46,225 --> 00:01:48,305
I'll be left with nothing.

18
00:01:49,345 --> 00:01:51,305
You weren't standing up for yourself.

19
00:01:51,385 --> 00:01:53,145
All you did was hurt someone

20
00:01:53,225 --> 00:01:55,145
and call it love.

21
00:01:57,225 --> 00:01:58,785
I only drove you back here

22
00:02:00,105 --> 00:02:01,825
because you're still my mother.

23
00:02:03,385 --> 00:02:04,865
But from now on,

24
00:02:04,945 --> 00:02:07,945
I won't take responsibility
for your actions anymore.

25
00:02:08,545 --> 00:02:10,385
What actions? I'm not scared.

26
00:02:12,745 --> 00:02:14,345
Well, I sure hope so.

27
00:02:15,225 --> 00:02:17,625
Because Neen definitely
won't let you get away with this.

28
00:02:20,705 --> 00:02:22,025
What's that supposed to mean?

29
00:02:25,545 --> 00:02:27,505
You attacked her today.

30
00:02:27,585 --> 00:02:29,705
There were witnesses and videos.

31
00:02:29,785 --> 00:02:31,425
The evidence is clear.

32
00:02:33,465 --> 00:02:35,025
Neen's not the quiet type,

33
00:02:35,585 --> 00:02:37,305
and she's no pushover.

34
00:02:37,905 --> 00:02:41,825
She's been putting up with you
out of respect for me.

35
00:02:41,905 --> 00:02:43,945
But what you did today

36
00:02:44,025 --> 00:02:46,745
was totally inhumane.

37
00:02:48,185 --> 00:02:49,545
In that case,

38
00:02:49,625 --> 00:02:51,665
I have nothing to lose now.

39
00:02:53,225 --> 00:02:54,545
I see you've made your choice.

40
00:03:23,945 --> 00:03:25,025
Neen,

41
00:03:25,625 --> 00:03:28,585
-can I go say hi to your parents?
-Don't.

42
00:03:40,345 --> 00:03:42,225
Let me talk to them first.

43
00:03:44,145 --> 00:03:45,345
You should go home.

44
00:03:53,185 --> 00:03:55,385
Then, feel free to call me…

45
00:03:57,225 --> 00:03:59,625
whenever you want to come home.

46
00:04:04,505 --> 00:04:05,585
Sure.

47
00:04:08,145 --> 00:04:09,265
You should get going.

48
00:04:46,065 --> 00:04:48,345
Yes, please take care of it for me.

49
00:04:49,505 --> 00:04:50,585
Thank you.

50
00:04:53,705 --> 00:04:55,585
I called the restaurant

51
00:04:55,665 --> 00:04:58,585
to ask everyone
who filmed the incident today

52
00:04:58,665 --> 00:05:00,385
not to publish the videos.

53
00:05:01,305 --> 00:05:04,065
They said they’d do their best to help.

54
00:05:06,145 --> 00:05:09,945
Do you want to go up and get some rest,
or should we put a cold pack on your face?

55
00:05:10,465 --> 00:05:12,705
We'll figure out what to do tomorrow.

56
00:05:16,945 --> 00:05:19,745
Take it easy and get some rest.

57
00:05:20,425 --> 00:05:24,025
As for the rest,
let me handle everything for you.

58
00:05:28,985 --> 00:05:30,185
Nai,

59
00:05:31,745 --> 00:05:33,825
please don't blame Runch for this.

60
00:05:35,585 --> 00:05:37,985
Mom and Dad want to blame her too.

61
00:05:38,745 --> 00:05:39,945
It's not just me.

62
00:05:40,665 --> 00:05:41,825
Then…

63
00:05:44,665 --> 00:05:47,465
can you two not blame her for this?

64
00:05:51,825 --> 00:05:53,265
I won't.

65
00:05:56,145 --> 00:05:57,825
I want you

66
00:05:58,545 --> 00:05:59,705
to divorce her.

67
00:06:04,625 --> 00:06:05,665
Honey…

68
00:06:09,865 --> 00:06:11,785
That's all I ask.

69
00:06:13,465 --> 00:06:14,705
Neen.

70
00:06:15,425 --> 00:06:17,305
We all love you.

71
00:06:22,145 --> 00:06:24,265
I've always taken good care of you.

72
00:06:25,025 --> 00:06:26,545
I can't stand

73
00:06:28,065 --> 00:06:30,145
seeing you get treated this way.

74
00:06:40,865 --> 00:06:44,665
I'm sorry for troubling you all.

75
00:06:49,665 --> 00:06:50,705
Neen,

76
00:06:51,545 --> 00:06:53,145
there's no need to apologize.

77
00:06:54,265 --> 00:06:55,625
You didn't do anything wrong.

78
00:07:01,825 --> 00:07:04,305
Look, I'm not forcing you.

79
00:07:05,905 --> 00:07:07,865
I want you to think it over.

80
00:07:09,665 --> 00:07:11,425
There might be a way

81
00:07:11,505 --> 00:07:13,585
to prevent Mrs. Ging
from doing this again.

82
00:07:18,305 --> 00:07:20,705
No matter what it takes,

83
00:07:20,785 --> 00:07:21,945
I'll try every way.

84
00:07:54,465 --> 00:07:56,305
When no one was around to trouble you,

85
00:07:56,385 --> 00:07:58,705
you were doing just fine, weren't you?

86
00:08:00,905 --> 00:08:01,905
Yeah.

87
00:08:08,745 --> 00:08:10,345
It was like a dream.

88
00:08:13,745 --> 00:08:16,945
It felt just like
when we were newly married.

89
00:08:23,465 --> 00:08:25,145
But it was just a dream.

90
00:08:27,505 --> 00:08:30,185
In the end,
I had to wake up and face reality.

91
00:08:33,945 --> 00:08:36,745
Nai and your dad
are taking this very seriously,

92
00:08:36,825 --> 00:08:38,505
so I'm sure she'll fold.

93
00:08:39,185 --> 00:08:41,625
Then, you can go back to being happy.

94
00:08:41,705 --> 00:08:44,985
But Runch has to let us
deal with that troublemaker.

95
00:08:45,065 --> 00:08:47,425
She will. She'll let us do anything.

96
00:08:48,105 --> 00:08:50,425
But Runch can't be truly happy

97
00:08:50,505 --> 00:08:53,185
if her parents are still in a tight spot.

98
00:08:57,825 --> 00:08:59,065
I understand.

99
00:09:02,185 --> 00:09:03,665
I mean…

100
00:09:05,065 --> 00:09:06,585
I just feel like

101
00:09:06,665 --> 00:09:10,185
there's no way for me and Runch
to be happy together.

102
00:09:18,825 --> 00:09:20,745
Maybe we should break up.

103
00:09:22,625 --> 00:09:23,705
Neen!

104
00:09:25,785 --> 00:09:27,265
Are you sure about that?

105
00:09:28,265 --> 00:09:29,265
Hmm?

106
00:09:32,345 --> 00:09:33,825
I don't know.

107
00:09:36,785 --> 00:09:40,305
I don't know anything. I'm just so tired.

108
00:09:43,945 --> 00:09:45,945
It's okay, honey.

109
00:09:46,025 --> 00:09:48,065
I really am.

110
00:09:48,145 --> 00:09:49,065
It's okay.

111
00:09:50,145 --> 00:09:51,785
There's no need to think yet.

112
00:09:52,425 --> 00:09:54,545
Okay, honey? Just get some rest.

113
00:10:00,905 --> 00:10:02,225
Easy now.

114
00:10:14,265 --> 00:10:17,145
MOTHER-IN-LAW IN HEATED FIGHT
WITH RICH DAUGHTER-IN-LAW

115
00:10:18,905 --> 00:10:21,025
<i>You shameless bitch.</i>
<i>You always act all nice</i>

116
00:10:21,105 --> 00:10:24,065
<i>and sweet, but you're just a selfish girl</i>

117
00:10:24,145 --> 00:10:25,665
<i>who wants to steal everything from others!</i>

118
00:10:26,945 --> 00:10:28,425
<i>If that's how you feel…</i>

119
00:10:28,505 --> 00:10:30,505
-Nai, what's that?
<i>-…then that's your problem, not mine.</i>

120
00:10:30,585 --> 00:10:31,545
<i>You crazy bitch!</i>

121
00:10:33,505 --> 00:10:34,705
Why the long face?

122
00:10:35,745 --> 00:10:36,985
Is something wrong?

123
00:10:38,705 --> 00:10:41,825
The videos from the restaurant
are being shared all over the internet.

124
00:10:44,305 --> 00:10:45,425
What?

125
00:10:45,505 --> 00:10:47,545
You said it was all under control.

126
00:10:47,625 --> 00:10:48,625
So, how come…?

127
00:10:53,505 --> 00:10:55,305
It'll be easy to find out who posted them.

128
00:11:03,185 --> 00:11:04,505
Hey, Utt.

129
00:11:04,585 --> 00:11:07,625
Did you hear? Our boss's mother
hit her daughter-in-law at a restaurant.

130
00:11:07,705 --> 00:11:08,985
It's crazy!

131
00:11:09,065 --> 00:11:11,225
Of course I did.
That's why I'm in a good mood.

132
00:11:12,785 --> 00:11:13,825
Utt,

133
00:11:13,905 --> 00:11:16,185
Mr. Apichet wants to see you now.

134
00:11:22,825 --> 00:11:24,905
You wanted to speak to me, Mr. Apichet?

135
00:11:37,465 --> 00:11:38,825
Surprised to see me?

136
00:11:43,465 --> 00:11:44,505
What do you want?

137
00:11:53,065 --> 00:11:54,345
You're fired, Utt.

138
00:11:56,345 --> 00:11:57,705
Fired?

139
00:11:57,785 --> 00:12:00,345
On what grounds? What did I do wrong?

140
00:12:02,105 --> 00:12:03,505
You seriously don't know?

141
00:12:11,305 --> 00:12:12,785
I know you did this.

142
00:12:16,905 --> 00:12:18,585
Do you have proof?

143
00:12:19,625 --> 00:12:21,785
If I didn't,
I wouldn't be saying all this.

144
00:12:23,625 --> 00:12:25,425
You have 30 minutes.

145
00:12:26,025 --> 00:12:27,905
Go pack up your things.

146
00:12:30,865 --> 00:12:32,465
Don't make me do this the hard way.

147
00:12:39,545 --> 00:12:43,145
You're going to regret your decision.

148
00:13:13,025 --> 00:13:13,945
Are you happy now?

149
00:13:15,425 --> 00:13:17,185
You got your case and the credit too.

150
00:13:17,825 --> 00:13:19,105
You won.

151
00:13:19,985 --> 00:13:21,385
You getting fired

152
00:13:21,465 --> 00:13:23,345
-had nothing to do with me.
-Yes, it did!

153
00:13:23,945 --> 00:13:25,145
If it weren't for you,

154
00:13:25,665 --> 00:13:27,145
this wouldn't have happened to me.

155
00:13:29,065 --> 00:13:30,745
You act all nice,

156
00:13:31,585 --> 00:13:33,105
as if you're the victim.

157
00:13:33,625 --> 00:13:35,985
But really,
I'm the victim you're trampling on!

158
00:13:36,705 --> 00:13:40,265
You brought this on yourself. All of it.

159
00:13:40,345 --> 00:13:43,105
So now you have to face the consequences.

160
00:13:43,785 --> 00:13:45,545
Screw you!

161
00:13:45,625 --> 00:13:47,665
I hope you're never happy.

162
00:13:47,745 --> 00:13:49,785
That you'll be alone
for the rest of your life.

163
00:14:13,785 --> 00:14:16,465
She hasn't said anything
since this morning.

164
00:14:23,465 --> 00:14:25,825
Maybe she's just figuring out

165
00:14:26,705 --> 00:14:28,345
what to do next.

166
00:14:32,105 --> 00:14:33,945
I'm just worried

167
00:14:34,025 --> 00:14:37,225
that she'll force herself to stay
so she doesn't lose anyone.

168
00:14:38,705 --> 00:14:40,505
What would you do if you were her?

169
00:14:43,665 --> 00:14:45,425
I just want her to be safe.

170
00:14:45,985 --> 00:14:48,505
Nothing matters more than that.

171
00:14:50,745 --> 00:14:52,665
This isn't Runch's fault, though.

172
00:14:52,745 --> 00:14:54,545
She loves our daughter too.

173
00:14:56,705 --> 00:14:57,985
You're right.

174
00:15:00,545 --> 00:15:03,545
But love alone won't fix anything.

175
00:15:11,625 --> 00:15:14,185
I wonder how she'll go about this.

176
00:15:20,825 --> 00:15:22,705
Whatever she decides,

177
00:15:24,065 --> 00:15:25,665
as her parents,

178
00:15:26,705 --> 00:15:29,305
we'll always welcome her back.

179
00:16:21,065 --> 00:16:22,185
Runch,

180
00:16:23,105 --> 00:16:24,465
did you see that shooting star?

181
00:16:26,665 --> 00:16:27,785
An actual shooting star--

182
00:16:50,225 --> 00:16:52,905
NEW MESSAGE FROM RUNCH

183
00:16:52,985 --> 00:16:55,185
<i>Did you eat yet?</i>

184
00:17:08,025 --> 00:17:09,145
NEEN

185
00:17:09,224 --> 00:17:12,704
<i>Not yet. What about you?</i>

186
00:17:15,944 --> 00:17:17,545
<i>I can't eat.</i>

187
00:17:17,625 --> 00:17:21,065
<i>I miss you too much.</i>
<i>I want you to come home.</i>

188
00:17:31,625 --> 00:17:33,825
<i>Please give me some more time, Runch.</i>

189
00:17:42,585 --> 00:17:46,785
<i>Okay, I understand. I can wait.</i>

190
00:17:46,865 --> 00:17:49,105
<i>No matter how long it takes,</i>
<i>I'll wait for you.</i>

191
00:21:05,625 --> 00:21:07,785
-Oh. Have a seat, honey.
-Neen.

192
00:21:07,865 --> 00:21:08,985
Come sit with us.

193
00:21:09,065 --> 00:21:10,265
Come on.

194
00:21:18,785 --> 00:21:22,025
This is Mr. Chuchai.
He is our company's lawyer.

195
00:21:23,225 --> 00:21:24,225
Good afternoon.

196
00:21:27,425 --> 00:21:28,785
I called him here

197
00:21:29,425 --> 00:21:31,705
so we can file a lawsuit
against Mrs. Gingkamol

198
00:21:31,785 --> 00:21:33,345
for assaulting you.

199
00:21:35,585 --> 00:21:36,505
A lawsuit?

200
00:21:40,225 --> 00:21:42,745
We can't let this slide.

201
00:21:42,825 --> 00:21:44,865
This time, it's not just a family matter.

202
00:21:46,385 --> 00:21:49,465
But, Dad, I don't want to sue her yet.

203
00:21:51,585 --> 00:21:52,705
Why not?

204
00:21:53,745 --> 00:21:56,185
We have evidence,
and she left visible marks on you.

205
00:21:56,265 --> 00:21:57,545
Why wouldn't you sue her?

206
00:21:58,825 --> 00:22:00,745
I didn't say I wouldn't.

207
00:22:01,465 --> 00:22:03,225
I'm just not ready yet.

208
00:22:03,785 --> 00:22:05,625
Can you give me some time?

209
00:22:06,505 --> 00:22:08,065
For what?

210
00:22:08,985 --> 00:22:11,065
For her to act this way again?

211
00:22:14,665 --> 00:22:16,385
I don't want you to live in fear

212
00:22:16,985 --> 00:22:18,865
and mistake it for patience.

213
00:22:21,625 --> 00:22:23,465
I know that, Dad.

214
00:22:23,545 --> 00:22:26,345
I just don't want things to escalate.

215
00:22:29,105 --> 00:22:30,985
I'm doing this to protect you.

216
00:22:35,345 --> 00:22:36,665
I know.

217
00:22:38,985 --> 00:22:42,505
But right now, I need some time
to process my emotions.

218
00:22:54,185 --> 00:22:55,945
-Neen.
-Honey. It's okay.

219
00:22:56,025 --> 00:22:57,425
I'll talk to her.

220
00:22:57,985 --> 00:22:58,985
Okay?

221
00:23:16,505 --> 00:23:17,905
Neen.

222
00:23:17,985 --> 00:23:20,545
Would you mind if I asked you something?

223
00:23:25,425 --> 00:23:27,705
Why won't you sue Mrs. Gingkamol?

224
00:23:33,425 --> 00:23:35,545
I'm not worried about the case.

225
00:23:37,745 --> 00:23:39,545
I'm worried about its consequences.

226
00:23:40,625 --> 00:23:42,105
Consequences for whom?

227
00:23:47,385 --> 00:23:48,505
For Runch.

228
00:23:58,265 --> 00:23:59,545
You see…

229
00:24:00,745 --> 00:24:02,665
if this continues,

230
00:24:02,745 --> 00:24:04,705
no matter what the verdict is,

231
00:24:05,385 --> 00:24:09,025
I'll be fine, but Runch will be crushed.

232
00:24:09,105 --> 00:24:11,745
After all, the culprit is her own mother.

233
00:24:13,185 --> 00:24:16,905
Her mother may be horrible and violent,

234
00:24:17,745 --> 00:24:20,745
but in the end, it's her who'll carry
the guilt for the rest of her life.

235
00:24:25,025 --> 00:24:29,505
I don't want to make her choose between
justice and being a good daughter

236
00:24:31,145 --> 00:24:34,625
even though she said
I could do whatever I want to her mother.

237
00:24:36,385 --> 00:24:39,345
What about you?
Who will make the choice for you?

238
00:24:43,265 --> 00:24:44,905
I am making that choice.

239
00:24:47,665 --> 00:24:51,065
Your dad and I never wanted you
to endure anything for anyone.

240
00:24:52,785 --> 00:24:54,105
I'm not.

241
00:24:56,385 --> 00:24:57,905
I just…

242
00:24:57,985 --> 00:25:01,065
want to do one last thing for Runch.

243
00:25:01,145 --> 00:25:02,825
Because on the day it happened,

244
00:25:03,345 --> 00:25:07,185
she defended me,
and her mother hit her too.

245
00:25:17,025 --> 00:25:18,905
I feel like…

246
00:25:22,545 --> 00:25:24,785
when she's with me…

247
00:25:27,345 --> 00:25:29,305
she seems miserable.

248
00:25:36,345 --> 00:25:38,185
What do you mean?

249
00:25:44,585 --> 00:25:45,785
I…

250
00:25:48,025 --> 00:25:50,065
I just want her to know that

251
00:25:51,585 --> 00:25:53,145
I may be hurt,

252
00:25:54,105 --> 00:25:57,625
but I won't let that ruin her life.

253
00:26:02,025 --> 00:26:05,625
I don't want her last memory of us

254
00:26:07,385 --> 00:26:10,425
to be me suing her mother.

255
00:26:13,385 --> 00:26:15,985
You're way too nice, Neen.

256
00:26:17,865 --> 00:26:19,985
I don't want to be nice.

257
00:26:21,145 --> 00:26:25,105
I just want us to break up
without hating each other.

258
00:26:32,505 --> 00:26:35,825
I don't know if you're making
the right decision,

259
00:26:36,985 --> 00:26:38,545
but I do know

260
00:26:40,145 --> 00:26:41,785
that it must be difficult for you.

261
00:26:53,465 --> 00:26:55,705
I still love her, Mom.

262
00:27:00,505 --> 00:27:02,825
I want to see her happy.

263
00:27:03,905 --> 00:27:07,985
It may be rough for a while
after we break up,

264
00:27:09,385 --> 00:27:10,305
but…

265
00:27:12,225 --> 00:27:14,625
if she can get through it,

266
00:27:16,745 --> 00:27:20,185
she might be happier
than when she's with me.

267
00:27:25,025 --> 00:27:26,185
Aw, honey…

268
00:28:03,185 --> 00:28:07,705
YOU HAVE A NEW MESSAGE

269
00:28:12,185 --> 00:28:14,265
<i>Let's meet at home this evening.</i>

270
00:28:23,265 --> 00:28:26,065
Have a seat. The food's still warm.

271
00:28:39,945 --> 00:28:42,065
These are from your restaurant.

272
00:28:43,185 --> 00:28:45,305
Is there a special occasion?

273
00:28:48,465 --> 00:28:49,585
No.

274
00:28:50,345 --> 00:28:52,545
I just wanted you to eat what you like.

275
00:28:54,745 --> 00:28:57,225
You really shouldn't have.

276
00:28:59,385 --> 00:29:01,585
Eat it while it's hot.

277
00:29:13,145 --> 00:29:14,425
You know,

278
00:29:16,025 --> 00:29:19,225
I remember all your likes and dislikes.

279
00:29:21,465 --> 00:29:23,825
I can even remember the day we first met

280
00:29:24,505 --> 00:29:26,145
three years ago.

281
00:29:29,265 --> 00:29:30,945
I remember too.

282
00:29:31,945 --> 00:29:33,945
We first met

283
00:29:34,825 --> 00:29:37,225
in the restroom at a coffee shop.

284
00:29:39,545 --> 00:29:41,745
You spilled coffee all over yourself.

285
00:29:43,025 --> 00:29:45,665
So you gave me a change of clothes,

286
00:29:46,185 --> 00:29:48,225
and we exchanged contact details.

287
00:29:51,825 --> 00:29:55,905
You know, I fell in love with you
the moment I saw you.

288
00:29:58,865 --> 00:30:01,465
I fell in love with your beauty

289
00:30:02,065 --> 00:30:03,665
and your smile.

290
00:30:08,465 --> 00:30:09,665
My heart

291
00:30:09,745 --> 00:30:12,705
beat so fast, it felt like it was
going to burst out of my chest.

292
00:30:14,985 --> 00:30:16,825
Me too.

293
00:30:18,025 --> 00:30:20,225
Your smile

294
00:30:20,305 --> 00:30:22,185
and your cheerful vibe

295
00:30:22,745 --> 00:30:25,425
got me dreaming every night

296
00:30:26,505 --> 00:30:28,705
that I'd get to see you every day.

297
00:30:36,145 --> 00:30:38,665
And then, that dream came true.

298
00:30:45,225 --> 00:30:47,265
We got married,

299
00:30:47,945 --> 00:30:49,425
and now we're living together.

300
00:30:55,545 --> 00:30:57,425
We get to see
each other's faces every day.

301
00:31:02,225 --> 00:31:03,985
I love you, Neen.

302
00:31:12,545 --> 00:31:14,545
I love you so much.

303
00:31:21,385 --> 00:31:23,065
I love you too.

304
00:31:28,385 --> 00:31:29,665
I love you the most.

305
00:31:41,385 --> 00:31:42,625
Runch.

306
00:31:50,985 --> 00:31:52,145
Yes?

307
00:32:02,585 --> 00:32:04,105
I want a divorce.

308
00:32:35,425 --> 00:32:36,825
Thank you

309
00:32:37,465 --> 00:32:39,825
for trying everything.

310
00:32:44,185 --> 00:32:46,265
I always knew

311
00:32:46,345 --> 00:32:49,745
you didn't want
any of those terrible things to happen.

312
00:32:50,625 --> 00:32:52,545
You had nothing to do with them.

313
00:33:07,385 --> 00:33:09,945
And I know

314
00:33:10,025 --> 00:33:13,545
you've been trying to save our marriage.

315
00:33:23,345 --> 00:33:24,865
Whatever you're thinking

316
00:33:26,545 --> 00:33:28,505
or feeling right now…

317
00:33:30,625 --> 00:33:32,105
can you tell me about it?

318
00:33:36,865 --> 00:33:38,305
I just

319
00:33:38,385 --> 00:33:41,985
don't want my love
to keep hurting you anymore.

320
00:33:44,465 --> 00:33:45,545
That's not true.

321
00:33:46,305 --> 00:33:47,545
It never did.

322
00:33:49,745 --> 00:33:52,825
Your love never hurt me, Neen.

323
00:33:55,785 --> 00:33:57,425
Runch, It's time to stop.

324
00:34:00,585 --> 00:34:02,625
You need to accept

325
00:34:02,705 --> 00:34:05,105
that no matter how hard we try,

326
00:34:05,185 --> 00:34:07,905
we can't escape
from the shadow of your mother.

327
00:34:13,425 --> 00:34:15,945
I'll give your mother what she wants.

328
00:34:17,784 --> 00:34:20,705
You can go back to being her daughter now.

329
00:34:22,225 --> 00:34:25,025
Let me do this one last thing for you.

330
00:34:56,025 --> 00:34:58,265
No matter what I say right now…

331
00:35:02,465 --> 00:35:05,185
I can't change your mind, can I?

332
00:35:10,505 --> 00:35:11,785
No.

333
00:35:19,585 --> 00:35:20,585
Okay.

334
00:35:28,185 --> 00:35:29,545
I understand now.

335
00:35:33,785 --> 00:35:35,225
Thank you

336
00:35:37,985 --> 00:35:40,345
for putting up with all of it for me.

337
00:36:13,105 --> 00:36:14,065
Neen!

338
00:36:17,065 --> 00:36:18,185
Neen!

339
00:36:24,425 --> 00:36:25,465
Neen!

340
00:36:26,985 --> 00:36:27,945
Neen!

341
00:36:29,425 --> 00:36:30,465
Neen.

342
00:36:35,385 --> 00:36:36,305
Yes?

343
00:36:38,345 --> 00:36:39,905
Where were you?

344
00:36:40,865 --> 00:36:43,305
I came downstairs to make you breakfast.

345
00:36:46,545 --> 00:36:48,065
Are you okay?

346
00:36:50,145 --> 00:36:52,585
I thought you'd leave me.

347
00:36:57,665 --> 00:36:59,345
I'll always be with you

348
00:37:00,185 --> 00:37:01,505
right there in your heart.

349
00:37:07,585 --> 00:37:08,425
Neen!

350
00:37:12,745 --> 00:37:13,985
Neen?

351
00:37:50,625 --> 00:37:51,825
Neen…

352
00:37:55,345 --> 00:37:56,505
Neen.

353
00:40:02,505 --> 00:40:03,545
Give me your hand.

354
00:40:03,625 --> 00:40:06,465
LAST YEAR

355
00:40:08,185 --> 00:40:11,465
Hold my hand and run along with me.

356
00:40:12,305 --> 00:40:14,665
I will never let go of your hand.

357
00:40:40,425 --> 00:40:43,625
Come to think of it,
relationships are pretty scary.

358
00:40:48,145 --> 00:40:50,065
What will you do

359
00:40:50,665 --> 00:40:51,745
if I get scared one day?

360
00:40:53,945 --> 00:40:57,225
I'll hold your hand like this…

361
00:41:00,305 --> 00:41:02,385
until you stop feeling scared.

362
00:41:11,105 --> 00:41:12,145
You promise?

363
00:41:18,265 --> 00:41:19,425
I promise.

364
00:41:33,105 --> 00:41:34,505
Here, put this on.

365
00:41:35,385 --> 00:41:36,745
It's windy.

366
00:41:36,825 --> 00:41:37,945
You'll catch a cold.

367
00:41:38,025 --> 00:41:39,145
Thank you.

368
00:41:41,825 --> 00:41:43,505
-Runch.
-Hmm?

369
00:41:45,185 --> 00:41:48,385
Can you be my happiness and mine alone?

370
00:41:49,025 --> 00:41:50,465
Of course.

371
00:41:50,545 --> 00:41:51,825
Forever.

372
00:42:09,865 --> 00:42:12,865
I want to take a picture for you.
You look so pretty today.

373
00:42:14,345 --> 00:42:15,425
Go for it.

374
00:42:23,665 --> 00:42:25,105
Don't look at the camera, though.

375
00:42:25,185 --> 00:42:26,985
Stare at the ocean

376
00:42:27,065 --> 00:42:29,465
as if you were thinking of something.

377
00:42:34,985 --> 00:42:36,345
Thinking of something?

378
00:42:36,425 --> 00:42:39,225
Can I think of you, then?

379
00:42:39,305 --> 00:42:40,585
Will the they turn out great?

380
00:42:42,265 --> 00:42:43,665
They are.

381
00:42:44,185 --> 00:42:46,345
They're so great

382
00:42:46,425 --> 00:42:48,225
that I'm getting distracted.

383
00:43:00,425 --> 00:43:01,305
Neen.

384
00:43:03,505 --> 00:43:06,425
You don't have to try to look sexy.

385
00:43:06,505 --> 00:43:07,825
You already caught my eye

386
00:43:07,905 --> 00:43:09,945
just with the way you are.

387
00:43:14,465 --> 00:43:15,425
Okay.

388
00:43:15,985 --> 00:43:17,785
Stunning.

389
00:43:18,385 --> 00:43:19,665
One, two, three.

390
00:43:21,345 --> 00:43:23,745
Got any good photos yet? Let me see.

391
00:43:25,145 --> 00:43:26,545
They're great.

392
00:43:26,625 --> 00:43:27,945
Here, let me show you.

393
00:43:28,985 --> 00:43:29,985
Aren't they great?

394
00:43:30,505 --> 00:43:31,825
Whoa!

395
00:43:31,905 --> 00:43:33,305
They're pretty great.

396
00:43:33,385 --> 00:43:34,465
Aren't they?

397
00:43:34,545 --> 00:43:35,985
I don't look like myself at all.

398
00:43:36,665 --> 00:43:40,025
I look like a whole different woman.

399
00:43:41,185 --> 00:43:42,865
No.

400
00:43:42,945 --> 00:43:44,505
It's still the same woman,

401
00:43:44,585 --> 00:43:47,625
but through the eyes
of someone who loves her.

402
00:43:49,265 --> 00:43:52,505
Then, can I be your model forever?

403
00:43:55,905 --> 00:43:57,425
Of course.

404
00:43:58,025 --> 00:43:59,465
Forever.

405
00:44:12,385 --> 00:44:14,505
Stop trying to control my life.

406
00:44:14,585 --> 00:44:16,985
And watch your life fall apart like this?

407
00:44:17,065 --> 00:44:19,825
My life isn't falling apart
because of Neen.

408
00:44:19,905 --> 00:44:23,065
If you still love Runch that much,
why divorce her?

409
00:44:23,145 --> 00:44:26,025
<i>Because she always sacrificed for me.</i>

410
00:44:35,425 --> 00:44:37,625
If the law can't punish someone like that,

411
00:44:37,705 --> 00:44:39,585
then we'll leave it to karma.

412
00:44:39,665 --> 00:44:41,185
You reap

413
00:44:41,265 --> 00:44:44,025
<i>what you sow.</i>

414
00:45:26,625 --> 00:45:29,025
Subtitle translation by:
Ramil Natnitiwitaya

